<p>I miss when a bunch of us weirdos overshared on our TiddlyWikis nearly every day. Most are gone or unmaintained now. Can we bring them back? I'll start: <a href="https://rudimentarylathe.org/">rudimentarylathe.org</a></p>
<!-- more -->
<p>Nearly 5,000 notes going back to 2018, and man oh man, at least 4,800 of them are an embarrassment. I should keep this stuff to myself, but that horse left the barn long ago.</p>
<p>We used to write &quot;TiddlyMails&quot; to each other (I don't think we actually called them that). I'd write a note that simply mentioned someone with their own wiki. They'd read it, and write a note on their wiki with a link back and a title something like: &quot;Re: That thing you wrote&quot;. It was completely manual and done without pings or notifications of any kind. So fun!</p>
<p>If you have a similar wiki, let me know. I'd love to visit!</p>
<p><a href="https://tiddlywiki.com/">TiddlyWiki</a> is more than 20 years old and still a miracle to me.</p>
